<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Rietberg</h1><p class="st-meta">1237 CE – 1807 CE (approx.) · capital Rietberg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tiny Westphalian county on the upper Ems that survived from 1237 to the Napoleonic era, last held by the Austrian statesman Kaunitz.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>A branch of the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnsberg">Arnsberg</a> established itself at Rietberg on the upper Ems around 1237, founding a small county in the marshy lowlands between the territories of Münster, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paderborn">Paderborn</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-ravensberg">Ravensberg</a>. The counts held it as an imperial fief.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The county was small and agricultural, with Rietberg as its only town. Through marriage it passed in the 16th century to the East Frisian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-cirksena">Cirksena</a> family and then, in 1699, to the Kaunitz family, whose most famous member, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wenzel-anton-von-kaunitz-rietberg">Wenzel Anton von Kaunitz-Rietberg</a>, became Austrian state chancellor under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a>. After a period of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a>, the county was restored to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rietberg was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-westphalia">Kingdom of Westphalia</a> in 1807 and passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1815, becoming part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/province-of-westphalia">Province of Westphalia</a>. The town of Rietberg is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-rietberg.jpg" alt="County of Rietberg" width="320" height="290"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_County_of_Rietberg_(1560).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1237 CE – 1807 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rietberg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wenzel Anton von Kaunitz-Rietberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Westphalian Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Germany</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rietberg</dd></dl></aside></div>
